{"content_hash": "5f12160989b3400b", "version_id": 385, "article_id": 39, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "Anthropic bans users from abusive behavior toward Claude", "title_zh": "Anthropic 禁止用户对 Claude 进行辱骂或残忍行为", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/08/anthropic-bans-abusive-behavior-claude", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784073829327-76999d522e45?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Nnx8YW50aHJvcGljJTIwYmFucyUyMHVzZXJzfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1NTMzNTF8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Brett Wharton on Unsplash", "author": "Brett Wharton", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@brettwharton?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-laptop-displaying-openai-40-chatbot-interface-YmSiFKOecCU?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(97, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(135, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "12a9c277b8fb"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 262, "reading_minutes": 1.3, "lead": "Anthropic has barred users from exhibiting sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior toward its models, as its leaders continue to ponder machine consciousness.", "lead_zh": "Anthropic 已禁止用户对其模型表现出持续且不必要的辱骂或残忍行为，与此同时，公司领导层仍在继续思考机器意识问题。", "preview": "The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson for Anthropic, the company behind the AI chatbot Claude, did not immediately resp", "preview_zh": "《The Verge》最先报道了这一政策变化。Anthropic 是 AI 聊天机器人 Claude 的幕后公司，其发言人没有立即回应关于什么可能被视为“辱骂或残忍”的询问。在一份在线用户政策中，这家总部位于旧金山的公司指出，其禁令不适用于常见的用户挫败感、模型测试或“黑暗创意主", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 375, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/39/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 105.388, "size_bytes": 636192, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 297, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/385.json", "paragraphs": ["The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson for Anthropic, the company behind the AI chatbot Claude, did not immediately respond to an inquiry about what could be considered abusive or cruel. In an online user policy, the San Francisco-based company noted that its ban would not apply to common user frustrations, model testing, or dark creative themes. Anthropic's usage policy previously contained restrictions on abusive conduct.", "The company's large language models have the ability to end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature rolled out last August, the company framed it as a safeguard for AI's welfare. \"We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs, now or in the future. However, we take the issue seriously, and alongside our research program we're working to identify and implement low-cost interventions to mitigate risks to model welfare, in case such welfare is possible. Allowing models to end or exit potentially distressing interactions is one such intervention,\" according to its website.", "The notion of AI systems being conscious has been highly polarizing in and outside the tech world. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has said he cannot rule out the possibility. Meanwhile, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared averse to the idea. \"I am very uncomfortable about people trying to ascribe religious force or a surrender of human judgment to AI models, and think it is a real safety issue,\" he wrote in an X post, days after the New York Times reported on Anthropic leaders' extensive conversations with religious scholars."], "paragraphs_zh": ["《The Verge》最先报道了这一政策变化。Anthropic 是 AI 聊天机器人 Claude 的幕后公司，其发言人没有立即回应关于什么可能被视为“辱骂或残忍”的询问。在一份在线用户政策中，这家总部位于旧金山的公司指出，其禁令不适用于常见的用户挫败感、模型测试或“黑暗创意主题”。Anthropic 的使用政策此前已包含对辱骂行为的限制。", "该公司的大型语言模型能够在用户持续有害时结束对话。当这一功能于去年八月推出时，公司将其标榜为对 AI 福祉的保障。根据其网站：“我们对 Claude 和其他大型语言模型现在或未来可能具有的道德地位仍高度不确定。然而，我们认真对待这一问题，并与我们的研究项目一起，努力识别和实施低成本干预措施，以降低模型福祉风险，以防这种福祉是可能的。允许模型结束或退出可能令人痛苦的互动就是其中一项干预措施。”", "AI 系统是否具有意识这一概念在科技界内外都极具两极分化。Anthropic 首席执行官达里奥·阿莫代伊曾表示，他不能排除这种可能性。与此同时，竞争对手 OpenAI 的首席执行官萨姆·奥尔特曼似乎反对这一想法。他在 X 上发帖写道：“我非常不安的是，人们试图将宗教力量或对人类判断的放弃归因于 AI 模型，并认为这是一个真正的安全问题。”几天前，《纽约时报》报道了 Anthropic 领导人与宗教学者的广泛对话。"], "body": "The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson for Anthropic, the company behind the AI chatbot Claude, did not immediately respond to an inquiry about what could be considered abusive or cruel. In an online user policy, the San Francisco-based company noted that its ban would not apply to common user frustrations, model testing, or dark creative themes. Anthropic's usage policy previously contained restrictions on abusive conduct.\n\nThe company's large language models have the ability to end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature rolled out last August, the company framed it as a safeguard for AI's welfare. \"We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs, now or in the future. However, we take the issue seriously, and alongside our research program we're working to identify and implement low-cost interventions to mitigate risks to model welfare, in case such welfare is possible. Allowing models to end or exit potentially distressing interactions is one such intervention,\" according to its website.\n\nThe notion of AI systems being conscious has been highly polarizing in and outside the tech world. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has said he cannot rule out the possibility. Meanwhile, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared averse to the idea. \"I am very uncomfortable about people trying to ascribe religious force or a surrender of human judgment to AI models, and think it is a real safety issue,\" he wrote in an X post, days after the New York Times reported on Anthropic leaders' extensive conversations with religious scholars.", "body_zh": "《The Verge》最先报道了这一政策变化。Anthropic 是 AI 聊天机器人 Claude 的幕后公司，其发言人没有立即回应关于什么可能被视为“辱骂或残忍”的询问。在一份在线用户政策中，这家总部位于旧金山的公司指出，其禁令不适用于常见的用户挫败感、模型测试或“黑暗创意主题”。Anthropic 的使用政策此前已包含对辱骂行为的限制。\n\n该公司的大型语言模型能够在用户持续有害时结束对话。当这一功能于去年八月推出时，公司将其标榜为对 AI 福祉的保障。根据其网站：“我们对 Claude 和其他大型语言模型现在或未来可能具有的道德地位仍高度不确定。然而，我们认真对待这一问题，并与我们的研究项目一起，努力识别和实施低成本干预措施，以降低模型福祉风险，以防这种福祉是可能的。允许模型结束或退出可能令人痛苦的互动就是其中一项干预措施。”\n\nAI 系统是否具有意识这一概念在科技界内外都极具两极分化。Anthropic 首席执行官达里奥·阿莫代伊曾表示，他不能排除这种可能性。与此同时，竞争对手 OpenAI 的首席执行官萨姆·奥尔特曼似乎反对这一想法。他在 X 上发帖写道：“我非常不安的是，人们试图将宗教力量或对人类判断的放弃归因于 AI 模型，并认为这是一个真正的安全问题。”几天前，《纽约时报》报道了 Anthropic 领导人与宗教学者的广泛对话。", "text": "The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson for Anthropic, the company behind the AI chatbot Claude, did not immediately respond to an inquiry about what could be considered abusive or cruel. In an online user policy, the San Francisco-based company noted that its ban would not apply to common user frustrations, model testing, or dark creative themes. Anthropic's usage policy previously contained restrictions on abusive conduct. The company's large language models have the ability to end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature rolled out last August, the company framed it as a safeguard for AI's welfare. \"We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs, now or in the future. However, we take the issue seriously, and alongside our research program we're working to identify and implement low-cost interventions to mitigate risks to model welfare, in case such welfare is possible. Allowing models to end or exit potentially distressing interactions is one such intervention,\" according to its website. The notion of AI systems being conscious has been highly polarizing in and outside the tech world. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has said he cannot rule out the possibility. Meanwhile, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared averse to the idea. \"I am very uncomfortable about people trying to ascribe religious force or a surrender of human judgment to AI models, and think it is a real safety issue,\" he wrote in an X post, days after the New York Times reported on Anthropic leaders' extensive conversations with religious scholars.", "vocab": [{"word": "barred", "pos": "verb", "zh": "禁止", "note": "常与 from 连用，如 bar sb from doing sth"}, {"word": "sustained", "pos": "adj", "zh": "持续的", "note": "强调长时间不间断"}, {"word": "needless", "pos": "adj", "zh": "不必要的", "note": "常含贬义，指无正当理由的"}, {"word": "abusive", "pos": "adj", "zh": "辱骂的；虐待的", "note": "abuse 的形容词形式"}, {"word": "cruel", "pos": "adj", "zh": "残忍的", "note": "比 harsh 语气更强"}, {"word": "ponder", "pos": "verb", "zh": "沉思；考虑", "note": "较正式，常接疑问从句"}, {"word": "inquiry", "pos": "noun", "zh": "询问；调查", "note": "英式拼写，美式为 inquiry"}, {"word": "persistently", "pos": "adv", "zh": "持续地；顽固地", "note": "修饰 harmful 等贬义形容词"}, {"word": "safeguard", "pos": "noun", "zh": "保障措施", "note": "常与 for/against 连用"}, {"word": "mitigate", "pos": "verb", "zh": "减轻；缓解", "note": "正式用词，常接 risks/effects"}, {"word": "distressing", "pos": "adj", "zh": "令人痛苦的", "note": "比 upsetting 更正式"}, {"word": "polarizing", "pos": "adj", "zh": "两极分化的", "note": "指引发强烈对立观点"}, {"word": "averse", "pos": "adj", "zh": "反对的；不乐意的", "note": "常与 to 连用，如 averse to risk"}, {"word": "ascribe", "pos": "verb", "zh": "把……归因于", "note": "常与 to 连用，如 ascribe sth to sb"}], "title_original": "Anthropic bans users from ‘needless abusive or cruel behavior’ towards Claude", "summary_original": "A spokesperson behind the tech company’s AI chatbot has not yet specified what counts as abusive or cruel content\nAnthropic has\nbarred users\nfrom exhibiting “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models, as the company’s leaders continue to ponder machine consciousness.\nThe Verge\nfirst\nreported the change in policy.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Anthropic bans users from ‘needless abusive or cruel behavior’ towards Claude\nA spokesperson behind the tech company’s AI chatbot has not yet specified what counts as abusive or cruel content\nAnthropic has\nbarred users\nfrom exhibiting “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models, as the company’s leaders continue to ponder machine consciousness.\nThe Verge\nfirst\nreported the change in policy.\nA spokesperson for\nAnthropic\n, which is behind AI chatbot Claude, did not immediately respond to an inquiry about what could be considered “abusive or cruel”.\nIn an online user policy, the San Francisco-based company noted that its ban would not apply to common user frustrations, model testing or “dark creative themes”.\nAnthropic’s usage policy previously contained restrictions on abusive conduct.\nThe company’s large language models have the ability to end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature rolled out last August, the company framed it as a safeguard for AI’s welfare.\n“We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs, now or in the future. However, we take the issue seriously, and alongside our research program we’re working to identify and implement low-cost interventions to mitigate risks to model welfare, in case such welfare is possible. Allowing models to end or exit potentially distressing interactions is one such intervention,” according to its website.\nThe notion of AI systems being conscious has been highly polarizing in and outside the tech world.\nAnthropic CEO Dario Amodei has\nsaid\nhe cannot rule out the possibility.\nMeanwhile, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared averse to the idea.\n“I am very uncomfortable about people trying to ascribe religious force or a surrender of human judgment to AI models, and think it is a real safety issue,” he wrote in an X post, days after the New York Times\nreported\non Anthropic leaders’ extensive conversations with religious scholars.\nExplore more on these topics\nAnthropic\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nChatbots\nDario Amodei\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T12:42:28.979686", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.263, "sm": 100, "em": 262, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Verge", "s": 0.275, "e": 0.625, "sm": 275, "em": 625, "cs": 4, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "first", "s": 0.637, "e": 0.938, "sm": 637, "em": 937, "cs": 10, "ce": 15, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "reported", "s": 0.95, "e": 1.4, "sm": 950, "em": 1400, "cs": 16, "ce": 24, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "the", "s": 1.413, "e": 1.488, "sm": 1412, "em": 1487, "cs": 25, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "policy", "s": 1.5, "e": 1.938, "sm": 1500, "em": 1937, "cs": 29, "ce": 35, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "change", "s": 1.95, "e": 2.525, "sm": 1950, "em": 2525, "cs": 36, "ce": 42, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": ".", "s": 2.525, "e": 3.388, "sm": 2525, "em": 3387, "cs": 42, "ce": 43, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "A", "s": 3.388, "e": 3.513, "sm": 3387, "em": 3512, "cs": 44, "ce": 45, "si": 1}, {"i": 9, "w": "spokesperson", "s": 3.525, "e": 4.25, "sm": 3525, "em": 4250, "cs": 46, "ce": 58, "si": 1}, {"i": 10, "w": "for", "s": 4.263, "e": 4.4, "sm": 4262, "em": 4400, "cs": 59, "ce": 62, "si": 1}, {"i": 11, "w": "Anthropic", "s": 4.412, "e": 5.062, "sm": 4412, "em": 5062, "cs": 63, "ce": 72, "si": 1}, {"i": 12, "w": ",", "s": 5.062, "e": 5.275, "sm": 5062, "em": 5275, "cs": 72, "ce": 73, "si": 1}, {"i": 13, "w": "the", "s": 5.275, "e": 5.375, "sm": 5275, "em": 5375, "cs": 74, "ce": 77, "si": 1}, {"i": 14, "w": "company", "s": 5.388, "e": 5.8, "sm": 5387, "em": 5800, "cs": 78, "ce": 85, "si": 1}, {"i": 15, "w": "behind", "s": 5.812, "e": 6.213, "sm": 5812, "em": 6212, "cs": 86, "ce": 92, "si": 1}, {"i": 16, "w": "the", "s": 6.225, "e": 6.325, "sm": 6225, "em": 6324, "cs": 93, "ce": 96, "si": 1}, {"i": 17, "w": "AI", "s": 6.338, "e": 6.688, "sm": 6337, "em": 6687, "